  "findings": [
    "Prefix cache: pure TTFT/prefill win on turns 2-3 (only the new suffix prefills). e.g. AR t3 ttft 356ms->20ms, DFlash t3 456ms->44ms; cached tokens grow 321->1042. AR decode tok/s is unchanged by the cache (~109.5 across all cache/turn cells).",
    "DFlash: lifts decode from ~109.5 tok/s (AR) to ~325 (t1) rising to ~400-448 (t3) at greedy, tracking tau 6.7->11.7 as later code-continuation turns get more predictable (~3x-4x).",
    "Sampling: AR greedy ~= AR sampled (~109.5; sampling overhead negligible). DFlash sampled is ~1.1-1.3x slower than greedy from lower acceptance (tau 5.8 vs 6.7 .. 9.5 vs 11.7) but DFlash STILL engages under sampling (tau 6-11), not an AR fallback."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Cells run AR-before-DFlash in a single interleave order; DFlash decode carries residual cool->hot thermal drift (playbook ~10-15% session drift). Medians reject the per-cell 3rd-rep throttle (visible in decode_tok_s_raw) but not a systematic trend. AR is stable.",
    "DFlash decode differences between cache on/off are confounded by trajectory + tau (cache-on/off follow different transcripts at temp=0) plus thermal ordering; they are NOT attributable to prefix caching. Only AR decode is a clean cache-invariant control.",
